{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Suddenly.</b> He revealed Himself to them suddenly, while they were in the midst of bodily functions, and they would cry out, 'Water, water!' — to inform them that Moses had done well to separate from his wife, since the Shekhinah was revealed to him constantly and there was no fixed time for the divine speech." "<b>Go out, the three of you.</b> This teaches that all three were called in a single utterance — something impossible for a mouth to say and an ear to hear at once. (Sifrei)"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:32.245681341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}